<h4>The e-value ledger</h4>
<p class="pnote">An e-value is a nonnegative payoff whose expectation under the null is at most 1.</p>
<table class="alt-table">
<thead><tr><th>Quantity</th><th>Meaning</th><th>Use</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td>E = 1</td><td>No net betting gain against the null</td><td>Starting point</td></tr>
<tr><td>E = 20</td><td>A twentyfold payoff from a bet fair under the null</td><td>Level-0.05 rejection threshold because 1 / 20 = 0.05</td></tr>
